sized different goals, processes of investigation, and standards of evidence.\\\"}, {\\\"title\\\": \\\"Epistemology - Wikipedia\\\", \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Epistemology\\\", \\\"snippet\\\": \\\"Epistemologists study the concepts of belief, truth, and justification to understand the nature of knowledge. To discover how knowledge arises, they investigate sources of justification, such as perception, introspection, memory, reason, and testimony.\\\"}, {\\\"title\\\": \\\"epistemic - Wiktionary, the free dictionary\\\", \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/epistemic\\\", \\\"snippet\\\": \\\"Philosophers differentiate the meanings of epistemic and epistemological. Broadly, epistemic means “relating to knowledge itself” [2] (see sense 1), and epistemological means “relating to the study or theory of various aspects of knowledge”. [3]\\\"}, {\\\"title\\\": \\\"EPISTEMIC Definition & Meaning | Dictionary.com\\\", \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://www.dictionary.com/browse/epistemic\\\", \\\"snippet\\\": \\\"EPISTEMIC definition: of or relating to knowledge or the conditions for acquiring it. See examples of epistemic used in a sentence.\\\"}, {\\\"title\\\": \\\"EPISTEMIC | definition in the Cambridge English Dictionary\\\", \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/us/dictionary/english/epistemic\\\", \\\"snippet\\\": \\\"In epistemic terms, it is unlikely that we could identify or verify such a cut-off point, even if it were to exist.\\\"}, {\\\"title\\\": \\\"Epistemic - definition of epistemic by The Free Dictionary\\\", \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://www.thefreedictionary.com/epistemic\\\", \\\"snippet\\\": \\\"Define epistemic. epistemic synonyms, epistemic pronunciation, epistemic translation, English dictionary definition of epistemic. adj. Of, relating to, or involving knowledge; cognitive. ep′i·ste′mi·cal·ly adv. American Heritage® Dictionary of the English Language, Fifth Edition....\\\"}, {\\\"title\\\": \\\"Epistemic - Definition, Meaning & Synonyms | Vocabulary.com\\\", \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://www.vocabulary.com/dictionary/epistemic\\\", \\\"snippet\\\": \\\"Definitions of epistemic adjective of or relating to epistemology “ epistemic modal” synonyms: epistemological\\\"}]}\", \"excerpt_truncated\": false, \"source_sha256\": \"7e16a76b71d60c9be48827a4b215ef7e8838a56dc55ffdbdb8041b896a58a6d2\", \"verification_required\": true, \"topic_domain\": \"judgment_and_consensus\", \"evidence_role\": \"discovery\", \"host_tier\": \"discovery\", \"source_identity\": null, \"persistent_identifiers\": [], \"source_candidates\": [\"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/epistemic\", \"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/us/dictionary/english/epistemic\"], \"source_candidate_identities\": {}}", "id": "source-4678bd20174a409c", "scope": "collected", "source": "https://www.bing.com/search?q=epistemic+deference+consensus+independent+judgment+evidence+reliability&format=rss"}, "prev_hash": "5865f7051c95558df9d0055d89e4c1bca2332daf216feb12ce1d3cd693c04fd0", "hash": "4bc2f8f2c813c169988df6ab17aa66b2428b2b5c06b1aec6eb20e1a0cf3dc5fd"}, {"seq": 615, "time": "2026-11-04T04:59:24.033055+00:00", "kind": "acquisition_assessed", "payload": {"domain": "creator_objective_critique", "evidence": "source-004a6bffb9374bfb", "outcome": "route_failure", "persistent_identifiers": [], "project": "proj-critique-001", "research_id": "immediate-f481afa369c20258", "route": "export.arxiv.org:discovery", "source_candidate_identities": {}, "source_candidates": [], "stage": "discovery"}, "prev_hash": "a6647340ecd5f7be22ed1fa9435808b1612561d77d1107284b4341545c1dd97c", "hash": "5865f7051c95558df9d0055d89e4c1bca2332daf216feb12ce1d3cd693c04fd0"}, {"seq": 614, "time": "2026-11-04T04:59:20.217304+00:00", "kind": "observation", "payload": {"actor": "collector", "content": "{\"url\": \"https://export.arxiv.org/api/query?search_query=all%3Aobjective+misspecification+goal+constraints+misalignment+reward+design&max_results=4\", \"error\"